statement:
Let $I$ be a directed set and $(X_i,f_{i'i})$ an inverse system of schemes [def-pc-scheme] over $I$ with affine transition morphisms [pqf-def-affine-morphism], every $X_i$ quasi-compact and quasi-separated [def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions], with limit $X=\varprojlim X_i$ and projections $f_i:X\to X_i$ [lem-weil-pbc-limit-affine-transition]. (Stacks states the lemma without the qcqs hypothesis; this node is the qcqs case, which the source proves first and which is the only case its users need.) For a scheme $T$ let $T_{affine,\Et}$ be the small affine etale site of [lem-weil-pbc-affine-etale-site-topos] (affine $U$ etale over $T$; coverings the standard etale coverings). For $i\le i'$ let $u_{i'i}:(X_i)_{affine,\Et}\to(X_{i'})_{affine,\Et}$, $V\mapsto V\times_{X_i}X_{i'}$, and $u_i:(X_i)_{affine,\Et}\to X_{affine,\Et}$, $V\mapsto V\times_{X_i}X$, be the base change functors (fibre products [def-pc-fibre-product]; $u_{ii}=\mathrm{id}$). Then:
(1) the $u_{i'i}$, $u_i$ are well defined (the base changes are affine and etale), continuous, and define morphisms of sites $(X_{i'})_{affine,\Et}\to(X_i)_{affine,\Et}$, $X_{affine,\Et}\to(X_i)_{affine,\Et}$ [def-weil-pbc-sites-and-cohomology]; they are compatible with composition up to the canonical isomorphisms $u_{i''i'}\circ u_{i'i}\cong u_{i''i}$, $u_{i'}\circ u_{i'i}\cong u_i$ of iterated fibre products, which satisfy the cocycle conditions; consequently, by [lem-weil-pbc-site-system-strictification], there are sites $\mathcal C_i$ with equivalences $e_i:(X_i)_{affine,\Et}\to\mathcal C_i$ preserving and reflecting coverings and strictly compatible continuous functors $u'_{i'i}:\mathcal C_i\to\mathcal C_{i'}$, $u'_i:\mathcal C_i\to X_{affine,\Et}$ ($u'_{i''i'}u'_{i'i}=u'_{i''i}$, $u'_{i'}u'_{i'i}=u'_i$) with $u'_{i'i}e_i\cong e_{i'}u_{i'i}$ and $u'_ie_i\cong u_i$, so that $(\mathcal C_i,u'_{i'i})$ over the cofiltered category $I^{\mathrm{op}}$ is a system of sites as in [lem-weil-pbc-colimit-of-sites] (standard etale coverings are finite);
(2) every affine $U$ etale over $X$ is isomorphic over $X$ to $u_i(U_i)$ for some $i$ and some $U_i$ in $(X_i)_{affine,\Et}$;
(3) for $U_i,V_i$ in $(X_i)_{affine,\Et}$, every morphism $u_i(U_i)\to u_i(V_i)$ over $X$ is $u_{i'}(\varphi)$ (up to the canonical isomorphisms) for some $i'\ge i$ and some morphism $\varphi:u_{i'i}(U_i)\to u_{i'i}(V_i)$ over $X_{i'}$, and two morphisms $\varphi,\psi:U_i\to V_i$ over $X_i$ with $u_i(\varphi)=u_i(\psi)$ satisfy $u_{i'i}(\varphi)=u_{i'i}(\psi)$ for some $i'\ge i$;
(4) the coverings of $X_{affine,\Et}$ are exactly the families isomorphic to images under some $u_i$ of standard etale coverings of $(X_i)_{affine,\Et}$;
(5) hence the functor $\varinjlim_i\mathcal C_i\to X_{affine,\Et}$ induced by the $u'_i$ on the colimit site of [lem-weil-pbc-colimit-of-sites] is an equivalence of categories under which a finite family is a covering of the colimit site if and only if its image is a covering of $X_{affine,\Et}$: $X_{affine,\Et}=\varinjlim_i(X_i)_{affine,\Et}$ as sites (Stacks Etale Cohomology, Lemma 0EYL).

